-- title:
--   Lemma 8, p.20 — $\|z^{k+1}-z_*^k\|\le\rho_k\tau_k$
-- statement:
--   Assume the standing assumptions of §3: $\varepsilon>0$, $\gamma_0>0$, $z^0\in\mathrm{dom}\,B$, $0<\delta<1$, $0<\nu\le1/2$, $\eta\in[0,\nu/(1+\nu))$, $\rho_0\ge1$, $0<\tau_0\le1$, $\zeta>1$, $0<\sigma<1/\zeta$, Assumption 1 with $\mu=0$, and let $x^*$ be an arbitrary fixed solution of (1). For every completed outer iteration $k$ of Algorithm 2, the point
--   $$
--   z_*^k=(I+\rho_k(F+B))^{-1}(z^k)
--   $$
--   exists, and
--   $$
--   \|z^{k+1}-z_*^k\|\le\rho_k\tau_k.
--   $$
--
--   So Algorithm 2 is an inexact proximal point method for $F+B$, with summable errors $\rho_k\tau_k$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: $F$ is a point-valued operator on $\mathrm{cl}(\mathrm{dom}\,B)$ → a total map on $\mathbb R^n$, constrained only on $\mathrm{cl}(\mathrm{dom}\,B)$; reason: values of $F$ elsewhere never enter $F+B$ or a run, since iterates lie in $\mathrm{dom}\,B$
--   - encoding: Assumption 1(d), the resolvent of $\gamma B$ can be exactly evaluated → a family $J$ with $J_\gamma=(I+\gamma B)^{-1}$ for every $\gamma>0$; reason: the assumption has no mathematical content; the family exists and is unique on $\gamma>0$
--   - encoding: iterates generated by Algorithm 2, $0\le k\in\mathbb K-1$ → the prefix predicate `Alg2.IsPrefix` at index $s$, with $k<s$; reason: $k\in\mathbb K-1$ says exactly that $z^{k+1}$ has been generated
--   - encoding: $z_*^k=(I+\rho_k(F+B))^{-1}(z^k)$, (67) → the relation $\rho_k^{-1}(z^k-w)\in(F+B)(w)$, with existence as a first clause and the bound for every such $w$; reason: (67) is that relation, and such a point is unique because $F+B$ is monotone
-- source:
--   Lu & Mei, Primal-dual extrapolation methods for monotone inclusions under local Lipschitz continuity, arXiv:2206.00973v3, Lemma 8, p.20, with (67)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ThreeOpSplitting_Convergence_MonotoneOperators
import Definitions.Def_MonoIncExtrap_Setting
import Definitions.Def_MonoIncExtrap_Algorithm1
import Definitions.Def_MonoIncExtrap_Algorithm2

open InnerProductSpace ThreeOpSplitting.Convergence

namespace MonoIncExtrap

/-- **Lemma 8.** arXiv:2206.00973v3, Lemma 8, p.20, with (67). For a run of Algorithm 2 and every
outer iteration `k` that has been completed, the point `z∗ᵏ = (I + ρ_k(F + B))⁻¹(zᵏ)` exists and
`‖z^{k+1} − z∗ᵏ‖ ≤ ρ_kτ_k` (69).

**Formalization Note.** (67) is the relation `IsResolventPoint`. Its existence is the first clause.
The bound is stated for every such point, and such a point is unique since `F + B` is monotone. -/
theorem lemma_8 {n : ℕ}
    {B : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))}
    {I : Alg2.Input (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} {xstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    (hI : Alg2.Standing B I xstar)
    {z : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} {c : ℕ → ℕ} {s : ℕ}
    (hz : Alg2.IsPrefix I z c s) {k : ℕ} (hk : k < s) :
    (∃ w, IsResolventPoint (I.rho k) (sumOp I.F B) (z k) w) ∧
    ∀ w, IsResolventPoint (I.rho k) (sumOp I.F B) (z k) w →
      ‖z (k + 1) - w‖ ≤ I.rho k * I.tau k := by sorry

end MonoIncExtrap
